---
/** What the framework does not do, said on the landing page and not only on the roadmap. */
import { href } from '../../lib/paths';

const LIMITS = [
  {
    title: 'No language server',
    text: 'The VS Code extension highlights .nexus files and has snippets. It does not complete or underline errors: type errors come from nexus check, in the terminal.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Nothing drives a game client',
    text: 'The Lua runtimes are tested in a real Lua 5.4 with stand-ins for the FiveM functions they use, and the example is started on a real server. No test plays the game.',
  },
  {
    title: 'No helpers for ESX, QBCore or Qbox',
    text: 'The runtimes are standalone. A handler calls the framework of the server itself.',
  },
  {
    title: 'One app per surface, and only LB',
    text: 'A resource has at most one phone app and one tablet app, in LB Phone and LB Tablet. No other phone or tablet resource is supported.',
  },
  {
    title: 'One answer per call',
    text: 'A call cannot be cancelled from the page and has no streaming answer. Progress is a push.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The contract has edges',
    text: 'No tuples, no recursive schemas, no binary payloads, and patterns are a subset of regular expressions.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section notyet" id="not-yet">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Not yet</span>
      <h2>What it does not do</h2>
      <p>
        This is version 0.2, and it is new. A feature is either in and documented, or it is on the roadmap: nothing is half done in
        the code. These are the limits you are most likely to meet.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="limits">
      {
        LIMITS.map((limit) => (
          <li class="reveal">
            <h3>{limit.title}</h3>
            <p>{limit.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost reveal" href={href('/docs/roadmap/')}>
      Read the whole roadmap
      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
